OL,3,GNEWSAExtreme weather leaves gardeners
OL,4,Ahedging their bets
OL,5,
OL,6,FGardeners in one of the most
OL,7,Fdrought-hit parts of the UK have said
OL,8,Fthey are adapting their planting
OL,9,Fstrategies amid increasingly extreme
OL,10,Fweather.
OL,12,FWest Sussex - like most of the country
OL,13,F- experienced an unprecedented summer
OL,14,Fmarked by record-breaking heatwaves and
OL,15,Fsevere drought.
OL,17,FThe conditions have put immense stress
OL,18,Fon many traditional plant species, with
OL,19,Fsome seriously struggling or dying
OL,20,Fcompletely.
OL,23,APub: 14-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,329,320,200,140,0,100
